  "notes": "PLAT-01 cycle 1: tracing-overhead calibration, not a figure. Second take. The first (2026-09-07-precision3591-investigation, max 75 us) was captured by a harness whose admission gate did not enforce the two-instrument rule, so it recorded excluded_from_series false on a traced run that can never feed the series; fixed in a646407 and re-taken rather than corrected in a footnote. The first capture is retained and published beside this one: its measurement was sound and only its admission field was wrong. The tracer was not re-armed between the two takes; the same armed state carried across, confirmed by nr-measure-mode status immediately before this launch. Event set armed and verified by scripts/nr-arm-trace.sh before the first run: sched:sched_switch sched:sched_wakeup irq:irq_handler_entry irq:irq_handler_exit timer:hrtimer_expire_entry workqueue:workqueue_execute_start ipi:ipi_send_cpu ipi:ipi_send_cpumask tlb:tlb_flush. tracing_cpumask 3fffff over all 22 logical cpus; buffer_size_kb 8195 per cpu (the kernel rounded up from 8192). Buffer verified non-empty on the isolated cores before launch: 2405 of 70460 lines came from cpus 6-11 at the report, 2414 nine lines later, the buffer being live; 2405 is the recorded verification count. breaktrace 100000 us, set far above anything plausible so it never fires and the run completes. Purpose is the traced baseline maximum M_traced, against M_untraced of 78 us from 2026-09-01-precision3591-calibration-clean, per the two-step calibration."
